        },
        {
            "block_label": "doc_title",
            "block_content": "PROBLEM 2A-8LEAKAGE PRESSURES FROM FULLY VENTED  THREE WALL CUBICLE ",
            "block_bbox": [
                276,
                282,
                1013,
                346
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Problem:Determine free-field blast wave parameters at a distance from a fully vented explosion inside a three wall cubicle.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                382,
                1034,
                433
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Procedure:",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                454,
                263,
                476
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 1.Determine charge weight, distance in the desired direction and volume of structure.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                499,
                1035,
                548
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 2.Apply a 20% safety factor to the charge weight.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                564,
                767,
                589
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 3.Calculate scaled distance and W/V ratio.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                603,
                700,
                626
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 4.Determine peak positive pressures using Figures 2-168 (+) or 2-169 (+).",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                641,
                1022,
                666
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 5.Determine maximum peak pressure for side and back directions from Figure 2-170 (+) using W/V ratio.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                680,
                994,
                730
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 6.For W/V ratio determine scaled positive impulses using Figures 2-171 (+)to 2-182 (+). Multiply by $W^{1/3}$ to calculate actual value of impulses.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                744,
                1036,
                796
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 7.Determine shock parameters from Figure 2-15 (+) corresponding to the peak pressure from Step 4, except for the normal reflected impulse where the scaled impulse from Step 6 should be used.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                809,
                1039,
                887
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "number",
